From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] plasma-dialer: choose the SIM of a call, show the SIM of the active call
Description:
 With more than one modem the dialer chose no modem ("TODO: select device
 uni"): dialling, USSD and the controls of the call screen did nothing.
 .
 SimUtils lists the active SIM of every modem with its slot
 (PrimarySimSlot, read over D-Bus), name ("SIM <slot>", else the operator
 name) and icon (shared with plasma-nm and spacebar in simidentitiesrc,
 class SimIdentities). The default SIM for calls is the SIM chosen for
 calls and text messages, kept by its ICCID in simidentitiesrc and shared
 with the cellular network settings and the messaging application (the
 settings page offers the same choice); without a choice it is the SIM in
 the first slot. With several SIMs the call button calls through the
 default SIM and carries the icon of that SIM as a badge; the so far empty
 cell left of it holds a smaller, tinted call button for the other SIM, or
 with three and more SIMs one that opens a choice. One tap is one call,
 nothing is remembered. USSD goes through the default SIM. In the call
 history the button at the end of an entry shows the icon of the SIM of
 the call instead of the handset, and calling back (tap on the entry or
 the button) goes through that SIM (the SIM identifier stored with each
 call). The call button of a contact carries the default SIM as badge,
 drawn as a disc in the text colour so that it stands out on the list. The
 call screen shows the icon and name of the SIM of the active call and
 controls the call through its modem (ActiveCallModel.account, the SIM
 identifier of the active call). With one SIM nothing changes.
 .
 Builds on the contacts and history patches (0002 and 0004 of this
 series).
Forwarded: no
License: as the patched files (LGPL-2.0-or-later, GPL-2.0-or-later, LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-GPL); new files simutils.*, CallButton.qml, SimBadge.qml LGPL-2.0-or-later, simidentities.* LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL
Last-Update: 2026-11-25
